# Repository workflow

Read `CONTRIBUTING.md` before opening an issue or pull request. Agents do not commit or push directly to `main`. The repository owner may.

- Open an issue when scope, ownership, or the desired outcome needs discussion.
- Open a pull request directly for a small, clear change. Use a draft pull request for early feedback.
- Link planned work with `Closes #<issue-number>`.
- Keep each pull request focused. Explain what changed, why, how it was verified, and whether timing, scheduling, records, or reported metrics changed.
- The assignee finishes the pull request. Request reviewers separately; assignment does not mean review.
- Merging requires one approval, code-owner review, resolved conversations, and a squash merge.
- GitHub branch protection enforces these rules for everyone except the repository owner.
